  "slug": "cargo-cytometry-a9cf",
  "summary": "Atlas-scale single-cell references and spatial co-mapping now reach 18M+ cells and near-cellular resolution within a single tissue section.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is spatially resolved and single-cell atlasing of human and mouse tissue, with each item extending cell-state or molecular maps into tissue architecture. A lifespan human lung reference integrates over 18M cells from 253 datasets into 142 cell types, including a rare intermediate alveolar population. A spatial and single-cell atlas of human cerebrovasculature profiles 1.5M cells and identifies vascular cell ensembles linked to disease risk. Spatial Hi-C-RNA co-maps 3D chromatin conformation and transcriptome from the same tissue section at near-single-cell resolution. Spaceland takes a different route, reconstructing continuous 3D gene-expression fields from sparse spatial transcriptomics and serial H&E histology. What is new is the pairing of chromatin and transcriptional readouts within one section, and the inference of volumetric expression from sparse sampling, rather than a shared organ or disease context.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-07-31"
}
